        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Hailey, Donna Tartt\n- Works: Hotel, Airport, Wheels, The Moneychangers, Overload, The Secret History, The Little Friend, The Goldfinch, Detective\n- Topics: bestselling novels, book sales, languages, authorship\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Hailey wrote the novel Hotel, which was published in 1965.\n- Arthur Hailey wrote the novel Airport, which was published in 1968.\n- Arthur Hailey wrote the novel Wheels, which was published in 1971.\n- Arthur Hailey wrote the novel The Moneychangers, which was published in 1975.\n- Arthur Hailey wrote the novel Overload, which was published in 1979.\n- Donna Tartt was born on December 23, 1963.\n- Arthur Hailey wrote the novel Detective.\n- Donna Tartt is an American writer.\n- Donna Tartt wrote the novel The Secret History, which was published in 1992.\n- Donna Tartt wrote the novel The Little Friend, which was published in 2002.\n- Donna Tartt wrote the novel The Goldfinch, which was published in 2013.\n- Arthur Hailey's meticulously researched books have sold 170 million copies in 38 languages.",
